+- Any rejection inside the turn calls `onError` with an `Error` — passed through when the thrown value is already an `Error`, or wrapped with a readable `message` with the original value as `cause` when a string, object or `undefined` is thrown, using a fallback message if string conversion throws — and then runs `afterSession` while still propagating the rejection to the caller ([validated by: calls onError with an Error carrying the thrown string and runs afterSession while rethrowing](../../src/orchestration/onErrorNonError.acceptance.test.ts#L53), [validated by: calls onError with an Error carrying a readable message when the stream rejects with a plain object](../../src/orchestration/onErrorNonError.acceptance.test.ts#L64), [validated by: preserves string, object and undefined rejections as the onError cause (specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md#8)](../../src/orchestration/onErrorCause.test.ts#L44), [validated by: preserves a rejection with no string conversion as the onError cause (specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md#8)](../../src/orchestration/onErrorCause.test.ts#L74)).
 
